  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much Maddie spent in total, we need to calculate the cost of the white T-shirts and the blue T-shirts separately, and then sum these amounts.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the cost of the white T-shirts:\n- Maddie bought 2 packs of white T-shirts.\n- Each pack of white T-shirts contains 5 T-shirts.\n- The cost of each T-shirt is $3.\n\nThe total number of white T-shirts is:\n\\[ 2 \\text{ packs} \\times 5 \\text{ T-shirts per pack} = 10 \\text{ T-shirts} \\]\n\nThe total cost for the white T-shirts is:\n\\[ 10 \\text{ T-shirts} \\times 3 \\text{ dollars per T-shirt} = 30 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the cost of the blue T-shirts:\n- Maddie bought 4 packs of blue T-shirts.\n- Each pack of blue T-shirts contains 3 T-shirts.\n- The cost of each T-shirt is $3.\n\nThe total number of blue T-shirts is:\n\\[ 4 \\text{ packs} \\times 3 \\text{ T-shirts per pack} = 12 \\text{ T-shirts} \\]\n\nThe total cost for the blue T-shirts is:\n\\[ 12 \\text{ T-shirts} \\times 3 \\text{ dollars per T-shirt} = 36 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nFinally, we sum the costs of the white T-shirts and the blue T-shirts to find the total amount Maddie spent:\n\\[ 30 \\text{ dollars} + 36 \\text{ dollars} = 66 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total amount Maddie spent is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{66}\n\\]",
